WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A splash of fresh water will reach the depths of your heart. Those mighty blue waves can propel you forward or they can calm and soothe. Coast to Michigan coast. Simply feel the flow in the moment. And let those vast lakes, rivers and streams create everlasting memories. Jump right in and let fresh wash over you in Pure Michigan. Keep it fresh at Michigan.org. Or on our website.
清凉的水花将流淌进你心灵深处。那些蔚蓝而澎湃的海浪能推动你前行，也能抚平你的心绪。漫步密歇根海岸。只需在此刻感受水流。让那些浩瀚的湖泊、河流和溪流留下永恒的回忆。纵身一跃，让纯净的密歇根之水洗涤你的心灵，尽在“纯粹密歇根”。请访问 Michigan.org 了解新鲜资讯。或访问我们的网站。

2
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Today's episode deals with a crime committed against a child that won't be suitable for all listeners. Today, the district of Notting Hill in London's inner west is renowned as one of the city's more affluent areas. But in the late 1940s, it was not a desirable place to live. A number of its buildings had been damaged or completely ravaged during the Blitz, an intensive German bombing campaign during the Second World War that killed more than 40,000 civilians. Many of the larger houses that remained standing were sold to landlords who divided them into multi-occupancy dwellings, with tenants leasing either a room or a single story. Ten Rillington Place in Notting Hill's Ladbrook Grove neighborhood was one such abode.
今天的节目讲述了一起针对儿童的犯罪，可能并非适合所有听众。如今，伦敦内西区的诺丁山街区以其较富裕的区域而闻名。但在20世纪40年代末，这里并不是一个理想的居住地。在二战期间德国的密集轰炸行动“闪电战”中，该地区的许多建筑遭到损坏或彻底摧毁，这场轰炸导致4万多平民丧生。许多幸存的大房子被卖给了房东，他们将其分割成多户住宅，租客们租下一间房或是一整层。诺丁山拉德布鲁克格罗夫社区的灵顿街10号就是这样一处住所。

3
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:42.000
It was the 10th house in a row of narrow, matching three-story brick residences situated at the end of a cul-de-sac that adjoined a busy thoroughfare named St. Mark's Road. All of the houses had been built during the 1870s and by the late 1940s they had fallen into neglect and disrepair. As they were home to so many residents, the street had a bustling atmosphere, with local children often gathering outside to play during the summer months. The landlord for number 10 lived elsewhere. They had split the house into three flats that each occupied an entire story of the building. It was poorly maintained and had no phone or indoor bathroom facilities.
它是死胡同尽头一排狭窄、相连且高三层的砖砌住宅中的第十栋，这条死胡同与一条名为圣马克路的繁华干道相连。所有的房子都建于19世纪70年代，到20世纪40年代末，它们已经年久失修、破败不堪。由于居住着大量居民，这条街充满了喧闹的氛围，当地的儿童经常在夏日聚在外面玩耍。10号的房东住在别处。他们将房子分成了三套公寓，每套公寓占据建筑的一整层。这里维护不善，没有电话或室内卫浴设施。

4
00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Instead, residents had to use bedpans or a lavatory in the backyard, which adjoined a small communal wash house. In March 1948, the property's ground and middle-floor flats were leased to long-term tenants, but the top floor remained available to rent. Newlyweds, Timothy and Beryl Evans had been living with Timothy's parents and sisters just around the corner on St. Mark's Road. Their living quarters were small and crowded. When Beryl discovered she was pregnant, she and Timothy decided it was time to find a place of their own. They were informed of a house nearby that had a sign in its top-floor window reading, Flat to Let. Its affordability, coupled with its convenient location near their extended family,
相反，居民们不得不使用便盆或后院的厕所，后院连着一个小型的公共洗衣房。1948年3月，这处房产的一楼和二楼公寓被租给了长期租客，但顶楼仍然空置待租。新婚夫妇蒂莫西和贝瑞尔·埃文斯曾与蒂莫西的父母和姐妹们住在圣马克路拐角处。他们的住所狭窄而拥挤。当贝瑞尔发现自己怀孕时，她和蒂莫西决定是时候找一个属于他们自己的地方了。他们听说附近有一栋房子，顶楼的窗户上挂着一块牌子，上面写着“公寓出租”。这里价格实惠，加上地理位置便利，靠近他们的大家庭，

5
00:03:34.000 --> 00:04:59.000
compelled the Evans' to submit an application, despite the property's less than desirable features. Their submission was approved, and on Monday, March 29, 1948, the young couple moved into 10 Rillington Place. Beryl, Susanna Thorley Beryl Susanna Thorley was born on September 19, 1929, in the south-east London area of Lewisham. She was the oldest of four children, with two younger brothers and a sister. During the Second World War, the Thorleys moved to the west London neighbourhood of Kensington. When Beryl's mother died in 1947, her father relocated to the Seaside Resort of Brighton, roughly 53 miles south of the capital. Beryl remained in London, where she worked as a telephone switchboard operator at Groverner House Hotel on Park Lane, a hotel in the upmarket district of Mayfair.
促使埃文斯夫妇提交了申请，尽管这栋房子的条件实在算不上理想。他们的申请获批，1948年3月29日星期一，这对年轻夫妇搬进了灵顿街10号。贝瑞尔，苏珊娜·索利，贝瑞尔·苏珊娜·索利于1929年9月19日出生于伦敦东南部的刘易舍姆。她是四个孩子中的老大，有两个弟弟和一个妹妹。二战期间，索利一家搬到了伦敦西部的肯辛顿社区。1947年贝瑞尔的母亲去世后，她的父亲搬到了位于首都以南约53英里海滨度假胜地布赖顿。贝瑞尔留在了伦敦，在梅菲尔高档区帕克巷的格罗夫纳豪房酒店担任电话总机接线员。

6
00:04:59.000 --> 00:06:14.000
One of her colleagues was dating a young man, who in turn offered to set Beryl up on a blind date with his friend. Timothy John Evans was born on November 20, 1924, in the Welsh mining town of Murther Tidville, located in the country's south. His father, who worked locally as a coal haulier, abandoned the family seven months before Timothy was born. As a result, Timothy and his older sister Eileen were raised by their mother, Thomasina. In 1929, she remarried another coal worker named Penry Probert. Later that year, the newlyweds had a daughter, Mary. Timothy Evans' childhood was marred by a number of developmental delays. He struggled to walk and speak, though eventually learned how to do both. At age eight, Timothy cut a toe on his right foot on some glass by a river. The wound was bandaged to using a dirty cloth, which led to him developing tubercular veruca, a rash of small, red, papula nodules related to the infectious disease tuberculosis.
她的一位同事当时正在和一个年轻男子交往，后者随后主动提出安排贝瑞尔和他的朋友进行一次盲相亲。蒂莫西·约翰·埃文斯于1924年11月20日出生于该国南部的威尔士采矿小镇迈瑟蒂德菲尔。他的父亲在当地做煤炭运输工，在蒂莫西出生前七个月抛弃了这个家庭。因此，蒂莫西和他的姐姐艾琳由母亲托马西娜抚养长大。1929年，她改嫁给另一个名叫佩里·普罗伯特的煤炭工人。同年晚些时候，这对新婚夫妇生了一个女儿玛丽。蒂莫西·埃文斯的童年伴随着多重发育迟缓。他学走路和说话都很艰难，不过最终还是学会了这两样。八岁时，蒂莫西右脚脚趾在河边被玻璃割伤。伤口用一块脏布包扎，导致他患上了结核性疣，这是一种与传染病结核病相关的、由小型红色丘疹组成的皮疹。

7
00:06:14.000 --> 00:07:33.000
The injury never healed properly, and Timothy was often in hospital receiving treatments. He missed out on much of his schooling, causing his literacy to suffer to the extent that he could barely write and could only read simple texts such as comic books. In 1935, when Timothy was ten years old, the Welsh coalfields were experiencing a depression, so his stepfather relocated to London in search of work. The rest of the family joined him six weeks later, settling in the cities in the West. Timothy continued to miss school due to his ill health. In 1939, he was sent to a clinic in Hampshire that specialized in treating children with tuberculosis and stayed for an entire year. Though the physicians there couldn't entirely fix Timothy's foot injury, they managed to treat it effectively enough that it never bothered him significantly again, though he was left with a permanent limp. By the time he reached adulthood, Timothy stood at five foot five inches tall and had a slight frame. Described as cocky and cheerful, he had dark eyes and dark hair, which he slicked back across his head.
这个伤口从未完全愈合，蒂莫西经常在医院接受治疗。他错过了大部分学业，导致识字能力严重受损，几乎不会写字，只能阅读漫画书等简单的文本。1935年，蒂莫西十岁时，威尔士煤田遭遇萧条，他的继父为了谋生搬到了伦敦。六个月后，其余家人也加入了他的行列，定居在西部的城市。由于身体健康状况不佳，蒂莫西继续缺课。1939年，他被送往汉普郡的一家诊所，该诊所专门治疗患有结核病的儿童，并在那里待了一整年。尽管那里的医生无法完全治愈蒂莫西的脚伤，但他们成功地进行了治疗，使其再也没有严重困扰过他，不过他留下了一个永久的跛足。到成年时，蒂莫西身高五英尺五英寸，身材瘦弱。他被形容为自负而开朗，有着黑色的眼睛和黑色的头发，头发向后梳理贴在头皮上。

8
00:07:33.000 --> 00:08:46.000
His leg impairment excused him from military service during World War II, and he remained in London with his family as the city endured the blitz. Although his limited education hindered his work prospects, he managed to secure a job as a car cleaner. Amongst friends and family, Timothy was renowned for exaggerating and telling tall tales. He'd developed the habit as a form of entertainment when he was bedridden as a child. He claimed that his father was an Italian count and that he had a brother who owned an enormous fleet of cars. Though he had a Welsh accent, he would sometimes feign a cockney manner of speaking to fit in with his English friends. Thomasina attributed her son's fibbing to his lack of self-confidence. If caught out in a lie, Timothy would become ashamed and would plead with his mother not to tell his older sister Eileen, whom he adored. In January 1947, shortly after Timothy's 22nd birthday, a friend offered to set him up on a date with a girl named Beryl Thorley.
由于腿部残疾，他在二战期间免于服兵役，并随着城市经受闪电战而与家人一起留在伦敦。尽管有限的教育限制了他的就业前景，但他还是找到了一份汽车清洗工的工作。在亲友中，蒂莫西以夸大其词和爱说大话而闻名。他在童年卧病在床时养成了这种作为消遣的习惯。他声称自己的父亲是一位意大利伯爵，自己还有一个拥有庞大车队的兄弟。尽管他带有威尔士口音，但他有时会假装伦敦腔，以融入他的英国朋友。托马西娜将儿子的谎言归咎于他缺乏自信。如果谎言被戳穿，蒂莫西会感到羞耻，并恳求母亲不要告诉他所崇拜的姐姐艾琳。1947年1月，在蒂莫西22岁生日后不久，一个朋友提出安排他和一个叫贝瑞尔·索利的女孩约会。

9
00:08:46.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Timothy was drawn to the petite, dark-haired Beryl, and the pair hit it off instantly. They met several more times to attend local dances and to go to the cinema. Within weeks of their first date, they became engaged. On September 20, one day after Beryl's 18th birthday, they married at Kensington Registry Office. Six months later, the couple moved into 10 Rillington Place in preparation of their growing family. Their flat consisted of a single bedroom with a joint living and kitchen space. Despite the cramped quarters and lack of modern amenities, they liked their new home and decided to stay put even when told of a ground floor flat available elsewhere that had its own garden and lavatory. Number 10 Rillington Place had several communal areas, including the hallway, staircase, and outside rear yard, so the evansers often saw their neighbours throughout the day.
蒂莫西被娇小、黑发的贝瑞尔所吸引，两人一拍即合。他们多次见面参加当地的舞会和去看电影。在第一次约会几周后，他们订婚了。9月20日，即贝瑞尔18岁生日的第二天，他们在肯辛顿登记处结婚。六个月后，为了迎接家庭新成员的到来，这对夫妇搬进了灵顿街10号。他们的公寓包括一间卧室以及连体的起居和厨房空间。尽管空间狭窄且缺乏现代设施，但他们还是喜欢这个新家，甚至在得知别处有一套带花园和厕所的一楼公寓空置时，也决定留在这里不搬走。灵顿街10号有几个公共区域，包括走廊、楼梯和外部后院，因此埃文斯夫妇整天都能看到邻居。

10
00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:49.000
The ground floor flat was home to another married couple, while the middle residence was occupied by an elderly man. Later that year, Timothy commenced a new job as a delivery driver for a food wholesaler. He managed to drive a van all over London, despite having difficulty reading signs and maps. On Sunday, October 10, 1948, Timothy and Beryl welcomed their firstborn, a girl they named Geraldine. Beryl was an affectionate mother, while Timothy spent hours playing with his daughter. He would bring her home small gifts that he collected throughout his delivery shifts. On Wednesday evenings, Thomasina would babysit her grandchild so that the new parents could go to the cinema together. Yet, their relationship grew increasingly fraught and difficult.
一楼的公寓住着另一对夫妇，而中间的住所则由一位老汉居住。同年晚些时候，蒂莫西开始了一份新工作，担任一家食品批发商的送货司机。尽管阅读路标和地图有困难，他还是设法开着货车跑遍了整个伦敦。1948年10月10日星期日，蒂莫西和贝瑞尔迎来了他们的长女，他们给她取名叫杰拉丁。贝瑞尔是一位慈爱的母亲，而蒂莫西则花好几个小时陪女儿玩耍。他会把在送货途中收集的小礼物带回家给女儿。星期三晚上，托马西娜会帮他们照看孙女，这样这对新手父母就可以一起去看电影了。然而，他们的关系却变得越来越紧张和艰难。

11
00:10:49.000 --> 00:11:42.000
Money was scarce. They struggled to afford rent and make repayments on their furniture. Timothy felt his wife did not know how to cook, clean, or manage a household budget. Beryl was frustrated at the amount of time and money her husband spent drinking at local pubs. He also had a quick temper that was exacerbated by alcohol. Their neighbours overheard their loud arguments, which sometimes became physical. By July 1949, Beryl had returned to work part-time to support her family. She struck up a mild flirtation with a colleague and once teased Timothy about it when he paid her a visit. He slapped her, and the pair caused a scene that resulted in Beryl losing her job.
资金匮乏。他们艰难地支付房租和家具的分期付款。蒂莫西觉得他的妻子既不会做饭、打扫卫生，也不会管理家庭预算。贝瑞尔则对丈夫花时间和金钱在当地酒吧喝酒感到沮丧。他还有暴躁的脾气，酒精更是加剧了这一倾向。邻居们无意中听到他们大声争吵，有时甚至演变成肢体冲突。到1949年7月，贝瑞尔为了补贴家用，已经恢复了兼职工作。她与一位同事产生了轻微的暧昧关系，当蒂莫西去看望她时，她还以此取笑蒂莫西。他打了她一巴掌，两人大闹了一场，结果贝瑞尔失去了工作。

12
00:11:42.000 --> 00:12:41.000
On another occasion, Beryl threw a jar of baby cream at her husband, causing a gash that required stitches. Beryl's father concluded that his daughter was unhappily married, and her relationship with Timothy was not, quote, a genuine friendship. Other relatives and acquaintances were of the opposite opinion, believing the couple were happy and in love. Timothy's younger sister, Mary, attributed their marital issues to struggling to make ends meet in post-war London. A young girl who babysat Geraldine described them as a lovely couple, very fond of each other. They did quarrel a bit, but never badly, and never for long. On the evening of August 28, 1949, a police officer was called to 10 Rillington Place following reports of a loud fight.
在另一次争吵中，贝瑞尔向丈夫扔了一罐婴儿面霜，导致他的一道伤口需要缝针。贝瑞尔的父亲断定女儿的婚姻并不幸福，她与蒂莫西的关系“算不上真正的友谊”。其他亲戚和熟人则持相反意见，认为这对夫妇很幸福且相爱。蒂莫西的妹妹玛丽将他们的婚姻问题归咎于战后伦敦勉强维生的挣扎。一个照顾过杰拉丁的小女孩形容他们是一对恩爱的夫妇，彼此非常喜欢。他们确实会吵点小架，但从不严重，也从不持久。1949年8月28日晚上，一名警察接到关于大声争吵的报警后，被召至灵顿街10号。

13
00:12:41.000 --> 00:13:33.000
In the top floor flat, they found Timothy, Beryl, Tomasina, and a teenage girl in the midst of an argument. The girl, 17-year-old Lucy Endicott, was a friend of Beryl's who was temporarily staying with the Evans''. Beryl had slapped Lucy after accusing her of sleeping with her husband the previous night. Tomasina was demanding Lucy leave as her presence was causing problems in her son's marriage. Lucy denied the allegations. She claimed to have witnessed Timothy beat Beryl and threatened to throw her out of a window. The feud ended with Lucy and Timothy leaving the flat. They stayed together for two nights until Lucy tired of his company and went home to her mother.
在顶楼公寓里，他们发现蒂莫西、贝瑞尔、托马西娜和一个十几岁的女孩正处于争吵之中。这个名叫露西·恩迪科特的17岁女孩是贝瑞尔的朋友，当时暂时借住在埃文斯夫妇家。贝瑞尔扇了露西耳光，指控她前一晚和自己的丈夫睡过觉。托马西娜要求露西离开，因为她的存在给她儿子的婚姻造成了问题。露西否认了这些指控。她声称目睹了蒂莫西殴打贝瑞尔，并威胁要把她扔出窗外。这场争端以露西和蒂莫西离开公寓告终。他们在一起待了两天，直到露西厌倦了他的陪伴，回家找她的母亲去了。

14
00:13:33.000 --> 00:14:40.000
Timothy returned to Beryl, who accepted him back. At around 7am on Tuesday, November 15, 1949, Cornelius Lynch was in the midst of preparing for work when he heard a knock on the front door. He was surprised to greet his 24-year-old nephew, Timothy Evans, the son of his sister, Tomasina. Timothy was far from home. Although he was born and raised in Southern Wales, he currently lived in London, 164 miles from Cornelius's house in the Welsh village of Murthervale. Timothy informed his uncle that he had been travelling with his boss searching for areas to expand his food wholesaler business. Their car broke down in the city of Cardiff, about half an hour's drive south, leaving them stranded for a few days at least. Cornelius and his wife, Violet, were happy to let their nephew stay with them for as long as he needed.
蒂莫西回到了贝瑞尔身边，而她接纳了他。1949年11月15日星期二早上7点左右，科尼利厄斯·林奇正在准备上班，突然听到前门传来敲门声。他惊讶地迎来了自己24岁的侄子蒂莫西·埃文斯，也就是他妹妹托马西娜的儿子。蒂莫西离家很远。尽管他在南威尔士出生长大，但他目前住在伦敦，距离科尼利厄斯在威尔士村庄迈瑟维尔的家有164英里远。蒂莫西告诉他的叔叔，他一直在和老板一起旅行，寻找扩大其食品批发业务的区域。他们的车在卡迪夫市抛锚了，卡迪夫在南面大约半小时车程的地方，这让他们至少滞留了几天。科尼利厄斯和他的妻子维奥莱特很高兴让侄子在他们家住多久都行。

15
00:14:40.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Timothy spent the following days going for walks in the nearby hills, reading comics by the fire and accompanying his aunt on shopping errands. A week-long absence from home would go unnoticed, as Beryl was holidaying at her widowed father's place in Brighton and had taken one-year-old Geraldine with her. A framed picture of the infant was displayed in the Lynch's house, and Timothy was often caught talking to it. On one occasion, he turned to his aunt, Violet, and told her, Just wait till you see her, Auntie Violet. She's a smasher. While at a pub with his nephew one day, Cornelius noticed Timothy holding what appeared to be a woman's wedding ring. When asked if it was Beryl's, Timothy said no, he'd just found it somewhere. He also gifted an old friend's wife a necklace, though didn't reveal where it had come from.
接下来的几天里，蒂莫西在附近的山丘上散步，在火炉旁读漫画书，并陪着姑姑去买杂货。由于贝瑞尔当时正在布赖顿她丧偶的父亲家度假，并且带上了一岁的杰拉丁，因此他离家一周并未引起注意。林奇家中摆放着婴儿的框装照片，蒂莫西经常被发现对着照片自言自语。有一次，他转身对姑姑维奥莱特说：“维奥莱特姑妈，等您见到她就知道了。她是个标致的小姑娘。”一天，科尼利厄斯和侄子在酒吧时，注意到蒂莫西手里拿着一件看起来像是女性结婚戒指的东西。当被问及这是不是贝瑞尔的时，蒂莫西说不是，他只是在什么地方捡到的。他还送给一个老朋友的妻子一条项链，但没有透露它是从哪里来的。

16
00:15:41.000 --> 00:16:44.000
On his fifth day in Murthervale, Timothy celebrated his 25th birthday. He left the following day of Monday, November 21, telling the Lynch's he needed to meet his boss in Cardiff to collect some pay and expenses. Three days later, Timothy reappeared. He admitted to his aunt and uncle that he never went to Cardiff, he had actually been back to London. When asked if he had seen his wife and daughter during his brief trip home, Timothy replied that he had. He revealed that Beryl had walked out on him and baby Geraldine. During his journey back to Murthervale, he dropped his daughter off with some acquaintances in the city of Newport, just outside of Cardiff. The Lynch's were suspicious of their nephew's odd behavior and confusing explanations and were not inclined to believe that Beryl had abandoned him and her baby.
在迈瑟维尔的第五天，蒂莫西庆祝了他的25岁生日。他在第二天11月21日星期一离开，告诉林奇一家他需要去卡迪夫见老板领取一些薪水和差旅费。三天后，蒂莫西重新出现。他向叔叔婶婶承认，他根本没去卡迪夫，实际上是回过伦敦。当被问及他在短暂的回家之行中是否见过妻子和女儿时，蒂莫西回答说见了。他透露贝瑞尔抛弃了他和婴儿杰拉丁。在返回迈瑟维尔的旅途中，他把女儿留在了卡迪夫郊外纽波特市的一些熟人那里。林奇夫妇对侄子古怪的行为和混乱的解释感到怀疑，并不倾向于相信贝瑞尔抛弃了他和孩子。

