00:19:03.000 --> 00:20:34.000
Yet, it had been almost a month since the otherwise communicative Beryl contacted her in-laws. Tomasina sent a telegram to Beryl's father in Brighton, as she had purchased a dress for Geraldine as a Christmas gift and wanted to confirm Beryl would still be there before sending it. In his reply, Beryl's father revealed that his daughter hadn't been staying with him. A short time later, Tomasina received a letter from her sister-in-law, Violet Lynch, informing her that Timothy had spent the previous two weeks at her home in Murthervale. A number of individuals told Tomasina that her son owed them money, leading her to suspect he had run away from his debts. Furious that Timothy was lying and had seemingly abandoned his responsibilities, Tomasina wrote back to Violet. She panned. There is some mystery about him. You can tell him from me. I never want to see him again as long as I live. He packed up a good job here. He is like his father. No good to himself or anybody else. Violet Lynch received Tomasina's letter the morning of Wednesday, November 30. She read it to Timothy at the breakfast table before accusing him of lying.
然而，原本很健谈的贝瑞尔已经快一个月没有联系她的公公婆婆了。托马西娜给贝瑞尔在布赖顿的父亲发了一封电报，因为她为杰拉丁买了一件衣服作为圣诞礼物，想在寄出之前确认贝瑞尔是否还在那里。在回信中，贝瑞尔的父亲透露他的女儿一直没有和他住在一起。不久后，托马西娜收到小姑子维奥莱特·林奇的一封信，信中告知蒂莫西在迈瑟维尔她的家度过了过去的两个星期。许多人告诉托马西娜她的儿子欠了他们钱，这导致她怀疑他是为了躲债而逃跑了。托马西娜对蒂莫西说谎且似乎抛弃了责任感到愤怒，她回信给维奥莱特。她写道：“他身上有些蹊跷。你可以替我转告他。只要我活着，就再也不想见到他了。他在这里辞掉了一份好工作。他跟他父亲一样，对自己和任何人都没用。”维奥莱特·林奇于11月30日星期三早晨收到了托马西娜的信。她在餐桌上读给蒂莫西听，然后指责他说谎。

20
00:20:34.000 --> 00:21:55.000
He maintained his story that Beryl and Geraldine were in Brighton. He also denied selling their furniture. He appeared anxious and didn't finish eating his meal. At 3.10 that afternoon, he walked into Murthervale's police station. Timothy told the officer on duty, Detective Constable Gwynfren Evans, I would like to have a chat with you alone. He was taken into the station's charge office, where he announced, I want to give myself up. I have disposed of my wife. When asked what he meant, Timothy elaborated. I put her down the drain. The detective queried whether Timothy knew what he was admitting to. He answered, Yes, I know what I'm saying. I can't sleep and want to get it off my chest. He was cautioned and asked if he wanted to make a written statement. As he couldn't read or write, Timothy suggested he talk about it while officers dictated. He was then transferred five miles north to the criminal investigation department in his hometown of Murther Tidville.
他坚持他先前的说法，坚称贝瑞尔和杰拉丁在布赖顿。他还否认卖掉他们的家具。他显得很焦虑，没有吃完饭。那天下午3点10分，他走进了迈瑟维尔的警察局。蒂莫西对值班警官、侦探警员格温弗伦·埃文斯说：“我想单独和您聊聊。”他被带到警察局的问询室，在那里他宣布：“我要自首。我处理掉了我的妻子。”当被问及这是什么意思时，蒂莫西详细解释道：“我把她顺着下水道扔下去了。”侦探询问蒂莫西是否知道自己在承认什么。他回答说：“是的，我知道我在说什么。我睡不着觉，想卸下心头大石。”他受到了警告，并被问及是否想做出一份书面记录。由于不会读写，蒂莫西建议他讲述，由警官口述记录。随后，他被向北转移了五英里，带到了他家乡迈瑟蒂德菲尔的刑事调查部。

