他恢复了第二份供词，指责约翰·克里斯蒂杀害了贝瑞尔，尽管没有证据表明她曾接受过失败的流产手术。他谈到约翰一定也杀害了杰拉丁。莫里斯警告他的当事人，法庭可能不会相信这一版本的事件，如果他坚持以此作为辩护，那么他将需要出庭作证。蒂莫西表示理解并欣然同意这样做。当时的英国法律实践意味着，即使被告被控多起谋杀，也只会因其中一起被起诉。因此，控方必须决定是以谋杀贝瑞尔还是杰拉丁的罪名来审判蒂莫西·埃文斯。

60
01:01:36.000 --> 01:02:47.000
In cases where two murders were tied together in a single event, evidence that related to the first murder could be given in a trial about the second, but not the other way around. After some consideration, they chose to proceed with trialling the accused for Geraldine's murder. This way, they could still enter evidence about Beryl's death into court, thus strengthening their case against him for the murder of Geraldine. The trial commenced on Wednesday, January 11, 1950, at the Central Criminal Court of England and Wales, commonly known as the Old Bailey. There was little media interest in the case, and it was barely covered by the daily papers. Before proceedings began at 1030, Timothy Evans' legal team were startled to learn that key witness for the prosecution, John Christie, had a criminal record. This was despite Chief Detective Inspector George Jennings stating that John's record was, quote, as white as the driven snow.
在两起谋杀案在单一事件中联系在一起的情况下，与第一起谋杀有关的证据可以在有关第二起谋杀的审判中提出，但反之则不然。经过一番考虑，他们选择继续对被告进行杰拉丁谋杀案的审判。通过这种方式，他们仍然可以将关于贝瑞尔死因的证据带入法庭，从而加强他们对他谋杀杰拉丁的指控。审判于1950年1月11日星期三在英格兰和威尔士中央刑事法院（通常被称为老贝利）开庭。媒体对该案兴趣不大，日报也几乎没有报道。在10点30分庭审开始前，蒂莫西·埃文斯的法律团队惊奇地得知，控方的关键证人约翰·克里斯蒂有犯罪记录。尽管侦探总督察乔治·詹宁斯曾声明约翰的记录是“洁白无瑕的”。

61
01:02:47.000 --> 01:03:51.000
Three decades earlier in 1921, John Christie stole two money orders during his employment as a postman, leading to a three-month prison sentence. Three years later, he committed larceny twice and was again sent to prison. The same year, he and Ethel separated, and John struck up a new relationship with a woman he met in London named Maude. Five years later, he was convicted of assaulting Maude after striking her in the head with a cricket bat. He was sentenced to six months' hard labour. His final conviction was for stealing a car in 1933, for which he served another three months. The prosecution and police were satisfied that John Christie had since become an upstanding citizen, worthy of testifying on their behalf in a murder trial. Following the outbreak of World War II, he worked as a war reserve constable until his resignation in 1943.
三十年前的1921年，约翰·克里斯蒂在担任邮递员期间偷了两张汇票，导致他被判处三个月监禁。三年后，他两次犯下盗窃罪，并再次被送进监狱。同年，他和埃塞尔分居，约翰与他在伦敦遇到的一位名叫莫德的女子开始了新的恋情。五年后，他在用板球棒击打莫德头部后被判犯有袭击莫德罪。他被判处六个月的苦役。他的最后一次定罪是在1933年偷窃一辆汽车，为此他又服刑三个月。检方和警方对约翰·克里斯蒂此后已成为一名正直的公民、有资格在谋杀审判中为他们作证感到满意。第二次世界大战爆发后，他一直担任战时预备警察，直到1943年辞职。

62
01:03:51.000 --> 01:05:15.000
He and wife Ethel had since reunited and had lived at 10 Grillington Place since 1938. Despite this, the defence regarded John Christie as an unreliable witness. When John was called to give evidence at trial, he gave detailed accounts of arguments he'd overheard between the evidences, painting their relationship as destructive. He claimed that on the evening of November 10, the night that the prosecution was alleging the accused had killed baby Geraldine, Timothy had arrived home, quote, extremely angry, upset, really wild. He told John that he had quit his job and was hoping to find a new one in Bristol, where Beryl and Geraldine supposedly were, and would be selling his furniture before leaving. Defence barrister Malcolm Morris cross-examined John, using the opportunity to share his defendants' explanation for both murders by stating, Well, Mr Christie, I've got to suggest to you, and I do not want there to be any misapprehension about it, that you are responsible for the death of Mrs Evans and the little girl.
他和妻子埃塞尔此后重聚，自1938年以来一直住在里灵顿广场10号。尽管如此，辩方仍将约翰·克里斯蒂视为不可靠的证人。当约翰被传唤在审判中作证时，他详细描述了他在证据之间无意中听到的争吵，将他们的关系描绘成具有破坏性的。他声称在11月10日晚上，即控方指控被告杀死小杰拉丁的那天晚上，蒂莫西到家时“极其愤怒、心烦意乱、非常疯狂”。他告诉约翰，他已经辞去了工作，希望能去布里斯托尔找一份新工作，贝瑞尔和杰拉丁据称就在那里，并打算在离开前卖掉他的家具。辩护大律师马尔科姆·莫里斯对约翰进行了交叉盘问，借此机会分享了被告对两起谋杀案的解释，他说：“好吧，克里斯蒂先生，我不得不向你提出，我不想对此产生任何误解，那就是你对埃文斯太太和小女孩的死负有责任。”

63
01:05:15.000 --> 01:07:01.000
While he acknowledged that he had known about Beryl's unwanted pregnancy, John firmly denied suggesting that he could perform an abortion for her. When asked whether he owned any medical textbooks, John said he owned a St John's ambulance manual that included diagrams of the human body, but had never shown it to Timothy Evans. He called the accusation that he helped carry Beryl's body downstairs ridiculous, as he had been bedridden with severe back pain and information of the small intestine during the week in question. In a final attempt to undermine John's credibility, Morris concluded his cross-examination by addressing his prior convictions. Other witnesses for the prosecution included Ethel Christie, whose testimony matched that of her husband's, Timothy's aunt, Violet Lynch, and Dr Robert Tear, the pathologist who had performed the autopsies of Beryl and Geraldine. He described how the pair were killed by strangulation and made it clear that there was no evidence of damage to Beryl's uterus indicative of an abortion procedure. All four of Timothy Evans' confessions were read to the court. The defense aimed to discredit them and managed to find one unreliable aspect. According to an inspector who was present at the time Timothy provided his statements, chief detective inspector George Jennings mentioned where Beryl and Geraldine's bodies were found before Timothy provided that information himself.
虽然他承认自己知道贝瑞尔的不想要怀孕，但约翰坚决否认曾暗示自己可以为她实施堕胎。当被问及他是否拥有任何医学教科书时，约翰说他拥有一本圣约翰救护手册，其中包含人体图解，但从未将其展示给蒂莫西·埃文斯。他称有关他协助将贝瑞尔的尸体抬下楼的指控是荒谬的，因为在相关的一周里，他一直卧床不起，患有严重的背痛和小肠炎症。为了最后一次削弱约翰的可信度，莫里斯通过谈及他先前的定罪结束了他的交叉盘问。控方的其他证人包括埃塞尔·克里斯蒂，她的证词与她丈夫的吻合；蒂莫西的姑姑维奥莱特·林奇；以及对贝瑞尔和杰拉丁进行尸检的病理学家罗伯特·蒂尔医生。他描述了两人是如何被勒死致死的，并明确表示没有证据表明贝瑞尔的子宫受到损伤可以证明曾进行过堕胎手术。蒂莫西·埃文斯的四份口供全部在法庭上宣读。辩方的目标是抹黑它们，并成功找到了一个不可靠的方面。据一位在蒂莫西提供口供时在场的督察称，侦探总督察乔治·詹宁斯在蒂莫西自己提供该信息之前就提到了贝瑞尔和杰拉丁的尸体是在哪里被发现的。

64
01:07:01.000 --> 01:08:26.000
The defense only had one witness, Timothy Evans. Timothy explained to the court that he had initially blamed a stranger he met in a cafe for Beryl's death in order to protect John Christie. Upon learning that her body wasn't in the storm drain as he believed it would be, he had decided to tell the truth. He described his latter two confessions as a load of lies that he'd made up because he was destroyed at learning of Geraldine's death and believed police would knock him about if he didn't comply. He stated that when police showed him his wife and daughter's clothing and the other artifacts found with their bodies, they also revealed that the pair had been in the wash house concealed by timber. In his final question to his client, Malcolm Morris asked, Had you anything left to live for when Geraldine was dead? Timothy replied, No sir. Prosecutor Christmas Humphries referred to the defendants' known and extensive history of lying. He described to John Christie, a World War I veteran who also worked in the War Reserve police during World War II as a perfectly innocent man who had no motive to murder his neighbors.
辩方只有一名证人，即蒂莫西·埃文斯。蒂莫西向法庭解释说，他最初为了保护约翰·克里斯蒂，将贝瑞尔的死归咎于他在咖啡馆遇到的一個陌生人。在得知她的尸体不在他以为的雨水渠中后，他决定说出真相。他将后两份口供描述为他编造的一堆谎言，因为他在得知杰拉丁的死讯时感到崩溃，并相信如果他不服从，警察会殴打他。他表示，当警察向他展示他的妻子和女儿的衣服以及随尸体发现的其他物品时，他们还透露说这两人一直在被木材遮挡的洗衣房里。在对他当事人的最后一个问题中，马尔科姆·莫里斯问：“当杰拉丁死后，你还有什么活下去的理由吗？”蒂莫西回答说：“没有，先生。”检察官克리스마스·汉弗里斯提到了被告已知且广泛的撒谎历史。他将约翰·克里斯蒂描述为一名一战老兵，在二战期间也在战时预备警察中工作过，是一个完全无辜的人，没有动机谋杀他的邻居。

65
01:08:26.000 --> 01:09:24.000
Humphries asked the defendant, Can you suggest why he should have strangled your wife? Can you suggest why he should have strangled your daughter? To both of these questions, Timothy replied, No. At the conclusion of his 10 minute long closing argument, Humphries asked the jury. Even if Christie had been responsible for the woman's death, why should he two days later go up to that flat and strangle an innocent little baby lying there aged 14 months? Even this fluent liar, who will lie as and when he pleases, cannot invent an answer to that question. The defense's closing argument was significantly longer. Malcolm Morris reminded the jury that unlike John Christie, Timothy Evans had no previous convictions for violent behavior.
汉弗里斯问被告：“你能解释一下他为什么要勒死你的妻子吗？你能解释一下他为什么要勒死你的女儿吗？”对于这两个问题，蒂莫西都回答：“没有。”在他长达10分钟的结案陈词结束时，汉弗里斯质问陪审团。即使克里斯蒂应对女人的死负责，为什么他两天后要走到那个楼上去勒死一个躺在那里的、14个月大的无辜婴儿呢？甚至连这个能随时随地随心所欲说谎的流畅骗子，也无法为这个问题编造出一个答案。辩方的结案陈词要长得多。马尔科姆·莫里斯提醒陪审团，与约翰·克里斯蒂不同，蒂莫西·埃文斯没有暴力行为的前科。

